<section class="principles section-rule">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Why formalize?</p>
        <h2>Research you can inspect<br>one inference at a time.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Formalization turns assumptions, definitions, and proofs into durable public objects. Every theorem is checked by Lean’s kernel and built on Mathlib’s mathematical foundations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="feature-index">01</span>
        <h3>Explicit assumptions</h3>
        <p>Formal statements make the exact economic environment and logical dependencies visible.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="feature-index">02</span>
        <h3>Reusable theory</h3>
        <p>General results can support new mechanisms, models, and research without reproving the foundations.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="feature-index">03</span>
        <h3>Machine checked</h3>
        <p>Lean verifies every proof term against a small trusted kernel, from definitions to final theorems.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="work section-rule">
  <div class="shell work-grid">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="kicker">Inside the library</p>
      <h2>From mechanism rules<br>to economic conclusions.</h2>
      <p>The current development begins with auction theory and expands into reusable single-parameter, pricing, probability, and game-theoretic foundations.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">See how the library is organized <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <ol class="layer-list">
      <li>
        <span class="layer-number">1</span>
        <div><h3>Mechanism</h3><p>Allocation and payment rules over participant reports.</p></div>
        <code>x, t</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="layer-number">2</span>
        <div><h3>Auction</h3><p>A mechanism together with types and a probabilistic environment.</p></div>
        <code>θ, ℙ</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="layer-number">3</span>
        <div><h3>Bidder problem</h3><p>The interim optimization problem faced by one participant.</p></div>
        <code>q, U</code>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

